    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2VvsAv9bMnVw5hmscGggixs)_\n\n## What\nThe posframe is a fixed 75% of the frame width again, for every command including `M-x`, instead of following the length of the prompt. This is the setup of #144 with no change: `sp-posframe-width-fraction` (0.75) and `sp-posframe-get-size`, which sets `:width`, `:min-width` and `:max-width` of the size from `vertico-posframe-get-size` and leaves the height to the package. It is wired in through `vertico-posframe-size-function`.\n\nNothing else comes back with it: no prompt styling, no dotted line, no dimming, no text size reset of the posframe. This is step 3 of the rebuild plan in the doc, taken as its own pull request so a bug points at one change.\n\nDocs (`sp-posframe.org`) and CHANGELOG updated.\n\n## Not tested\nNothing was run in Emacs (none in the container). The glitch's cause was never found and this size function was active in #144 to #154. If it returns, remove the `vertico-posframe-size-function` line first.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiBs9srTW9kUiGXduSF",
